      "hints": [
        "Substitute $\\cos^2\\theta = 1 - \\sin^2\\theta$ to obtain a quadratic in $\\sin\\theta$.",
        "Factorise the quadratic $(5\\sin\\theta - 1)(\\sin\\theta + 1) = 0$.",
        "Solve for $\\theta$ in the interval $\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Substitute the identity $\\cos^2\\theta = 1 - \\sin^2\\theta$ into the equation:\n$$5(1 - \\sin^2\\theta) = 4\\sin\\theta + 4 \\implies 5 - 5\\sin^2\\theta = 4\\sin\\theta + 4$$",
        "Rearrange into standard quadratic form:\n$$5\\sin^2\\theta + 4\\sin\\theta - 1 = 0$$",
        "Factorise the quadratic in $\\sin\\theta$:\n$$(5\\sin\\theta - 1)(\\sin\\theta + 1) = 0 \\implies \\sin\\theta = \\frac{1}{5} = 0.2 \\quad\\text{or}\\quad \\sin\\theta = -1$$",
        "Solve $\\sin\\theta = 0.2$ in $\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi$ (second quadrant):\n$$\\theta_1 = \\pi - \\sin^{-1}(0.2) \\approx \\pi - 0.20136 \\approx 2.94\\text{ rad}$$",
        "Solve $\\sin\\theta = -1$ in $\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi$:\n$$\\theta_2 = \\frac{3\\pi}{2} \\approx 4.71\\text{ rad}$$",
        "State all solutions in the given domain:\n$$\\theta = 2.94, \\quad 4.71\\quad\\left(\\text{or } \\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)$$"
      ],
